From bc58dcdffaf59db3ed00effbd1ca5fbbf1e9c479 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 01:08:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] language: the HDMI 1.4 notice says that the new modes are
 taken without a restart

The notice of a TV input in its HDMI 1.4 mode (#39995, in Estuary #31693)
told the user to turn on the enhanced HDMI format of the input and then
restart the system: Kodi kept the modes it read at its start. It takes the
display's new modes by itself now, a few seconds after the hot-plug event of
the TV, once nothing plays (CWinSystemGbm::RefreshModes()), so the notice says
that instead of the restart. Where they cannot be taken, a notice of its own
says to restart (#39957).

In en_gb first; es_ES, es_AR and es_MX in Estuary.
---
 addons/resource.language.en_gb/resources/strings.po           | 2 +-
 .../skin.estuary/language/resource.language.en_gb/strings.po  | 2 +-
 .../skin.estuary/language/resource.language.es_ar/strings.po  | 4 ++--
 .../skin.estuary/language/resource.language.es_es/strings.po  | 4 ++--
 .../skin.estuary/language/resource.language.es_mx/strings.po  | 4 ++--
 5 files changed, 8 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/addons/resource.language.en_gb/resources/strings.po b/addons/resource.language.en_gb/resources/strings.po
index cd9b718..02b1a93 100644
--- a/addons/resource.language.en_gb/resources/strings.po
+++ b/addons/resource.language.en_gb/resources/strings.po
@@ -25965,7 +25965,7 @@ msgstr ""
 #. Hades: notification when an HDR TV input is in its HDMI 1.4 compatibility mode; translated in Estuary (#31693)
 #: xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbm.cpp
 msgctxt "#39995"
-msgid "This HDMI input is in HDMI 1.4 mode: full-quality 4K only up to 30 Hz. For 4K at 50 and 60 Hz, turn on the enhanced HDMI format of this input in the settings of the TV or AV receiver (LG: HDMI Deep Colour), then restart the system."
+msgid "This HDMI input is in HDMI 1.4 mode: full-quality 4K only up to 30 Hz. For 4K at 50 and 60 Hz, turn on the enhanced HDMI format of this input in the settings of the TV or AV receiver (LG: HDMI Deep Colour). The new modes are picked up automatically a few seconds after the TV changes, while nothing is playing."
 msgstr ""
 
